# Every Dockerfile in this repository builds from the REPOSITORY ROOT and does
# `COPY . .`, so this file decides what ends up inside nine images.
#
# Two reasons it is load-bearing, both found by actually building:
#
#   1. Without it, the host's node_modules is copied over the one installed in
#      the image. On Windows that means native Windows binaries landing in an
#      Alpine container, and `pnpm build` fails its dependency check before it
#      compiles anything.
#   2. Without it, envs/.env.development is copied into an image layer. That file
#      holds JWT_PRIVATE_KEY, which signs every token in the system. A secret in
#      a layer is disclosed to anyone who can pull the image, and deleting it in
#      a later layer does not remove it.

# --- the two that break the build and leak a key -----------------------------
**/node_modules
envs/.env
envs/.env.*
!envs/.env.example

# --- build output. Rebuilt inside the image; copying it in is stale and slow --
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- version control and CI. Not needed at build time ------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- documentation. Large, and no service reads it ---------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md

# --- local tooling and editor state ------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.claude
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- other Dockerfiles and compose files -------------------------------------
# A Dockerfile does not need its siblings, and excluding them keeps an edit to
# one from invalidating every other image's cache.
docker/compose
**/Dockerfile
!docker/Dockerfile
